# Look and feel

One system. Pages do not pick their own colors, type, or spacing.

## Tokens

Define brand, type, space, and radius once in `src/styles/main.css` using Tailwind 4 `@theme`. Components use those tokens (`bg-surface`, `text-ink`, `font-display`), never raw hex after tokens exist.

Direction: quiet industrial B2B. Light surfaces, dark ink, one accent. Generous whitespace. Strong headings, short body. No playful display fonts, neon gradients, glassmorphism, or app-chrome (DaisyUI).

## Chrome

- Every page: `SiteHeader` + `SiteFooter` via `PageShell`.
- One max-width container (`AppContainer`). Do not nest extra centered wrappers.
- Section vertical rhythm from a shared scale (e.g. `py-16 md:py-24`), not one-off padding.
- Type scale shared: eyebrow, h1, h2, body, caption. Headings through `AppHeading`.
- Buttons only through `AppButton`: `primary`, `secondary`, `ghost`. One size scale.
- Links that are buttons use `AppButton`; text links use `AppLink` (Vue Router, same URL shape as canonicals).

## Motion and media

- Subtle transitions. Honor `prefers-reduced-motion`.
- Images: real operations photography, explicit width/height, lazy below the fold, modern formats (WebP/AVIF). No unlabeled stock.

## Responsive

Mobile-first Tailwind. Header, hero, and footer must work at a phone width and a desktop width. Verify both when layout changes.

## Accessibility

Semantic landmarks (`header`, `main`, `footer`, `nav`). Visible focus rings (do not `outline-none` without a replacement). Contrast that meets WCAG AA. Do not ship `v-html` of untrusted strings.
